From ae2c0002287e9fb98adfc5111feac7ad8fcdbb84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:02:34 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v5 09/10] wifi: rtw89: honor ASSIGN_SEQ and NO_ACK for
 injected frames

For injected frames, rtw89_core_tx_update_injection() only applies
the radiotap rate. Two more TX flags are ignored:

- The management path sets hw_ssn_sel/hw_seq_mode, and MLO links set
  upd_wlan_hdr, so the hardware overwrites the sequence number that
  user space put into the injected frame even though mac80211 did not
  request IEEE80211_TX_CTL_ASSIGN_SEQ.
- IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK (e.g. radiotap IEEE80211_RADIOTAP_F_TX_NOACK)
  does not limit retries, so a frame that will never be acknowledged
  is retransmitted up to the default retry limit.

Clear the hardware sequence settings unless ASSIGN_SEQ is set, and
limit NO_ACK frames to a single transmission attempt.

Signed-off-by: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
index 94610e3..428f347 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
@@ -1259,6 +1259,19 @@ static void rtw89_core_tx_update_injection(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 	desc_info->use_rate = true;
 	desc_info->dis_data_fb = true;
 
+	/* keep the sequence number supplied by user space */
+	if (!(info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_ASSIGN_SEQ)) {
+		desc_info->upd_wlan_hdr = false;
+		desc_info->hw_ssn_sel = 0;
+		desc_info->hw_seq_mode = 0;
+	}
+
+	/* no ACK is expected, so do not retry */
+	if (info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK) {
+		desc_info->tx_cnt_lmt_en = true;
+		desc_info->tx_cnt_lmt = 1;
+	}
+
 	/* No rate was given in the radiotap header. Management frames
 	 * already carry the rate from rtw89_core_tx_update_mgmt_info(), so
 	 * only data frames need a fallback.
